; TEST: expect-exit=100
;
; `arborea 1` IS `ordinata`, and the definition makes that a theorem rather
; than a coincidence: with w = 1 every contribution fills the group at once,
; the "tree" over one cell is that cell, so acc = op(acc, v) per contribution
; in contribution order -- which is `ordinata`'s rule verbatim. The count is
; reset by every contribution, so no tail can ever exist, and `redfin` emits
; no tail dispatch at all (emit.inc's __bfa_emit_redfin skips it below w = 2).
;
; Checked on the values that make the two shapes DIFFER at w = 8 --
; red_arborea_f32.ir's twenty (1.0f then nineteen halves-of-an-ulp, whose
; `arborea 8` answer is 0x3F800009) -- so this is not a fixture that would
; pass for any lowering: the same inputs, w = 1, must give the ORDINATA bits.
;
;   1  arborea 1 over the twenty  = 1.0  0x3F800000  (= ordinata)
;   2  ordinata over the twenty   = 1.0  0x3F800000  (the same run, again,
;                                        so the equality is checked here and
;                                        not across two fixtures)
;
; Mutation (run): the group tree taken over w cells regardless of how many
; are live, reading slots[1..w) of an uninitialised region -> exit 1 with
; whatever the frame held. The count not reset after a full group -> the
; second contribution writes slots[1] of a one-cell region, which is the
; `count` word itself, and the run never terminates the way it should:
; exit 1.
;
; CROSS-CHECKED THROUGH THE C BACKEND, 2026-09-27. This fixture carried
; `c-emit-exit=4` from the day it landed: the C backend refused the three
; reduction opcodes, so the differential phase could only check parity of a
; refusal. It carries the key no longer -- `backend_c/emit_c.inc` lowers
; `redinit`/`contrib`/`redfin`, and the four builds (gcc and clang, -O0 and
; -O2, every one under `-fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all`) are
; held to the SAME directive above as the reference's own run. The reference's
; verdict here is unchanged and has been since the day it landed; what is new
; is that three more toolchains have to agree with it.
;
; What this one cross-checks in particular: that the C lowering skips the tail
; dispatch below w = 2 as well. `__bfc_emit_redfin` makes the same test at the
; same place as `__bfa_emit_redfin`, so `arborea 1` emits no dispatch in
; either backend and the theorem above is a property of both.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = slot 8 8
%2 = fconst f32 1065353216
%3 = fconst f32 864026624
%4 = redinit f32 fadd arborea 1
contrib %4 %2
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
contrib %4 %3
%5 = redfin f32 %4
store f32 %1 0 nativus %5
%6 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%7 = iconst u32 1065353216
%8 = cmp.eq u32 %6 %7
br %8 b2 b1
b1:
%9 = iconst u8 1
ret %9
b2:
%10 = redinit f32 fadd ordinata 0
contrib %10 %2
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
contrib %10 %3
%11 = redfin f32 %10
store f32 %1 0 nativus %11
%12 = load u32 %1 0 nativus
%13 = cmp.eq u32 %12 %6
br %13 b4 b3
b3:
%14 = iconst u8 2
ret %14
b4:
%15 = iconst u8 100
ret %15
}
